id: DRAFT-7341-libtiff-4.7.2.2-jbig-codec-strip-only-api
category: consumer-api, codec, libtiff, testing
build_system: cmake|conan
phase: testing|runtime
match_keywords: libtiff, JBIG, TIFFWriteScanline, TIFFReadScanline, TIFFWriteEncodedStrip, TIFFReadEncodedStrip, ROWSPERSTRIP, scanline encoding is not implemented, scanline decoding is not implemented, encoderow, decoderow, JPEGCOLORMODE, pseudo-tag, Unknown pseudo-tag 65538, COMPRESSION
error_signature: "ISO JBIG scanline encoding is not implemented|ISO JBIG scanline decoding is not implemented|Unknown pseudo-tag 65538|Unknown pseudo-tag.*JPEGCOLORMODE"
error_excerpt: "A functional roundtrip probe exercising libtiff's JBIG codec failed on-device with 'ISO JBIG scanline encoding is not implemented' when writing via TIFFWriteScanline and 'ISO JBIG scanline decoding is not implemented' when reading via TIFFReadScanline; setting TIFFTAG_JPEGCOLORMODE before TIFFTAG_COMPRESSION failed with 'Unknown pseudo-tag 65538'. These are libtiff consumer-API constraints, not device failures — the same errors reproduce on a plain Linux build."
root_cause: "libtiff's JBIG codec registers only strip-level entry points: tif_jbig.c installs encodestrip/decodestrip but leaves encoderow NULL, so TIFFWriteScanline falls into the _TIFFNoRowEncode fallback (tif_compress.c); decoderow keeps the _TIFFNoRowDecode stub from TIFFDefaultDirectory. The JBIG encoder additionally requires the whole image in exactly ONE strip (JBIGSetupEncode checks rowsperstrip==height). JPEG's JPEGCOLORMODE is a pseudo-tag registered by the JPEG codec itself, so it is unknown to the directory machinery until the codec is attached (write) or the directory is read (read); the error string is 'Unknown %stag' (tif_dir.c), so the literal tag number never appears in the message."
rec_approach: "Use strip-level APIs for JBIG both ways: set TIFFTAG_ROWSPERSTRIP=height (single strip), allocate rowbytes*height, write with TIFFWriteEncodedStrip(t, 0, buf, n) and read with TIFFReadEncodedStrip(t, 0, buf, n). Set TIFFTAG_JPEGCOLORMODE AFTER TIFFTAG_COMPRESSION on write, and after the first TIFFGetField (which triggers the directory read) on read."
solution: "test_package/test.c in archives/l/libtiff/4.7.2.2: write_jbig1 uses a single-strip buffer + TIFFWriteEncodedStrip; verify_jbig1 reads the whole strip with TIFFReadEncodedStrip; JPEGCOLORMODE ordering fixed on both sides. On-device conan test result: 83/83 assertions green, including the JBIG and JPEG roundtrips (the scanline variant was 74/77)."
fallback: "If generic consumer code must stay on scanline APIs, treat JBIG as unsupported there (skip or convert to a scanline-capable codec) — the row-level entry points are simply not registered by the codec."
prescan_pattern: "JBIG|TIFFWriteScanline|TIFFReadScanline|JPEGCOLORMODE|pseudo-tag"
verify_builds: "libtiff 4.7.2.2 (task 7341): 真机 conan test 83/83 PASS（含 JBIG/JPEG 往返）；本地 MinGW 同款探针 28/28 PASS"
severity: 2
last_updated: 2026-09-26
